WEBVTT

00:00:00.057 --> 00:00:07.613
01 · Start from scratch. Flutter screens are built one widget at a time.

00:00:07.613 --> 00:00:15.553
02 · Properties changes appearance. Set the heading to 32 pixels and bold.

00:00:15.553 --> 00:00:24.857
03 · A Row is like flex-row. Add words and an icon inside the same parent.

00:00:24.857 --> 00:00:30.253
Placement follows the parent layout. Left moves this icon before the text.

00:00:30.253 --> 00:00:44.658
04 · Add a button, then connect an action. A label alone does not create behavior.

00:00:44.658 --> 00:00:56.037
05 · Check the same design on a tablet and PC. Expand canvas gives you more room.

00:00:56.037 --> 00:01:02.600
06 · Export the complete project. The ZIP includes Dart, web setup, and VS Code settings.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:05.801
Open the extracted folder in VS Code. Follow the setup guide before publishing.

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:11.678
Publish my app walks through build/web → local preview → your Cloudflare URL.

00:01:11.678 --> 00:01:14.522
Save wrangler.jsonc beside pubspec.yaml. Continue with the written publishing steps.
